-- ===========================================================================
-- tests-fees.l4 — the Fees Regulations in their three vintages, and the
-- SimpLEX scenarios run against every vintage, asserting what EACH VINTAGE
-- ACTUALLY ANSWERS. Every expected value is read off the source text cited
-- beside it. The table's own expectations that do not hold for the
-- Regulations as made or as amended are in tests-simplex-red.l4.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — the Fees Regulations`

§§ `Regulation 1 — which exams each vintage defines`

#ASSERT `regulation 1 defines` `a practical exam` `in` `the draft`
#ASSERT `regulation 1 defines` `a theoretical exam` `in` `the draft`
#ASSERT `regulation 1 defines` `a practical exam` `in` `the regulations as made`
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 1 defines` `a theoretical exam` `in` `the regulations as made`
#ASSERT `regulation 1 defines` `a practical exam` `in` `the regulations as amended`
#ASSERT `regulation 1 defines` `a theoretical exam` `in` `the regulations as amended`

§§ `Regulation 2 — the fee for each service under each vintage`

-- A theoretical exam: draft 2(א) 273; as made, silent; as amended 2(א1) 158.
#ASSERT `the fee for` (`taking` `a theoretical exam`) `under` `the draft` EQUALS JUST 273
#ASSERT `the fee for` (`taking` `a theoretical exam`) `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the fee for` (`taking` `a theoretical exam`) `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS JUST 158

-- A practical exam: draft 2(ב) 194; as made and as amended 2(א) 194.
#ASSERT `the fee for` (`taking` `a practical exam`) `under` `the draft` EQUALS JUST 194
#ASSERT `the fee for` (`taking` `a practical exam`) `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS JUST 194
#ASSERT `the fee for` (`taking` `a practical exam`) `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS JUST 194

-- An objection to a theoretical-exam grade: draft 2(ג) 40; as made, silent;
-- as amended 2(ב) 40.
#ASSERT `the fee for` (`an objection to the grade of` `a theoretical exam`) `under` `the draft` EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the fee for` (`an objection to the grade of` `a theoretical exam`) `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the fee for` (`an objection to the grade of` `a theoretical exam`) `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS JUST 40

-- An objection to a practical-exam grade: draft 2(ג) 40; as made 2(ב) 40; as
-- amended, silent — KT 12383 confined 2(ב) to "הבחינה העיונית".
#ASSERT `the fee for` (`an objection to the grade of` `a practical exam`) `under` `the draft` EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the fee for` (`an objection to the grade of` `a practical exam`) `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the fee for` (`an objection to the grade of` `a practical exam`) `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS NOTHING

-- A licence or its renewal under s. 5: 284 in every vintage (draft 2(ד),
-- otherwise 2(ג)).
#ASSERT `the fee for` `a licence, or the renewal of one, under section 5` `under` `the draft` EQUALS JUST 284
#ASSERT `the fee for` `a licence, or the renewal of one, under section 5` `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS JUST 284
#ASSERT `the fee for` `a licence, or the renewal of one, under section 5` `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS JUST 284

-- A temporary licence for a foreign expert: 398 in every vintage (draft 2(ה),
-- otherwise 2(ד)).
#ASSERT `the fee for` `a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or the renewal of one, under section 9` `under` `the draft` EQUALS JUST 398
#ASSERT `the fee for` `a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or the renewal of one, under section 9` `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS JUST 398
#ASSERT `the fee for` `a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or the renewal of one, under section 9` `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS JUST 398

-- A course under s. 17: s. 59 allows a fee; no vintage sets one.
#ASSERT `the fee for` `a continuing-training course under section 17` `under` `the draft` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the fee for` `a continuing-training course under section 17` `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the fee for` `a continuing-training course under section 17` `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 2 — which sub-regulation sets each fee`

#ASSERT `the sub-regulation that sets the fee for` (`taking` `a practical exam`) `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS JUST "2(א)"
#ASSERT `the sub-regulation that sets the fee for` (`taking` `a theoretical exam`) `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS JUST "2(א1)"
#ASSERT `the sub-regulation that sets the fee for` (`an objection to the grade of` `a practical exam`) `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS JUST "2(ב)"
#ASSERT `the sub-regulation that sets the fee for` (`an objection to the grade of` `a theoretical exam`) `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS JUST "2(ב)"
#ASSERT `the sub-regulation that sets the fee for` `a licence, or the renewal of one, under section 5` `under` `the draft` EQUALS JUST "2(ד)"
#ASSERT `the sub-regulation that sets the fee for` `a licence, or the renewal of one, under section 5` `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS JUST "2(ג)"
#ASSERT `the sub-regulation that sets the fee for` `a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or the renewal of one, under section 9` `under` `the draft` EQUALS JUST "2(ה)"
#ASSERT `the sub-regulation that sets the fee for` `a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or the renewal of one, under section 9` `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS JUST "2(ד)"

-- What the licence fee is charged on.
#ASSERT `what the licence fee is charged on under` `the draft` EQUALS `the application for the licence or its renewal`
#ASSERT `what the licence fee is charged on under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS `the receipt of the licence or its renewal`
#ASSERT `what the licence fee is charged on under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS `the receipt of the licence or its renewal`

§§ `Regulation 4 — the SimpLEX scenarios against every vintage`

-- Row 5, theoretical exam, 273 paid.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 5 — registration for a theoretical exam` `under` `the draft` EQUALS `not withheld: the fee set for the service was paid in full`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 5 — registration for a theoretical exam` `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS `not reached: no fee is set for the service`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 5 — registration for a theoretical exam` `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS `not withheld: the fee set for the service was paid in full`

-- Row 6, practical exam, 194 paid.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 6 — registration for a practical exam` `under` `the draft` EQUALS `not withheld: the fee set for the service was paid in full`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 6 — registration for a practical exam` `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS `not withheld: the fee set for the service was paid in full`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 6 — registration for a practical exam` `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS `not withheld: the fee set for the service was paid in full`

-- Row 7, an appeal with 40 paid, on each exam.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 7 — an appeal with payment of 40, on a theoretical exam` `under` `the draft` EQUALS `not withheld: the fee set for the service was paid in full`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 7 — an appeal with payment of 40, on a theoretical exam` `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS `not reached: no fee is set for the service`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 7 — an appeal with payment of 40, on a theoretical exam` `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS `not withheld: the fee set for the service was paid in full`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 7 — an appeal with payment of 40, on a practical exam` `under` `the draft` EQUALS `not withheld: the fee set for the service was paid in full`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 7 — an appeal with payment of 40, on a practical exam` `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS `not withheld: the fee set for the service was paid in full`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 7 — an appeal with payment of 40, on a practical exam` `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS `not reached: no fee is set for the service`

-- Row 8, an exam with nothing paid, on each exam.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 8 — registration for a theoretical exam without payment` `under` `the draft` EQUALS `withheld: the fee set for the service was not paid in full`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 8 — registration for a theoretical exam without payment` `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS `not reached: no fee is set for the service`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 8 — registration for a theoretical exam without payment` `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS `withheld: the fee set for the service was not paid in full`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 8 — registration for a practical exam without payment` `under` `the draft` EQUALS `withheld: the fee set for the service was not paid in full`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 8 — registration for a practical exam without payment` `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS `withheld: the fee set for the service was not paid in full`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `row 8 — registration for a practical exam without payment` `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS `withheld: the fee set for the service was not paid in full`

-- The worked example, theoretical exam, nothing paid.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `the worked example — a candidate registers for a theoretical exam but does not pay the fee` `under` `the draft` EQUALS `withheld: the fee set for the service was not paid in full`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `the worked example — a candidate registers for a theoretical exam but does not pay the fee` `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS `not reached: no fee is set for the service`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `the worked example — a candidate registers for a theoretical exam but does not pay the fee` `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS `withheld: the fee set for the service was not paid in full`

§§ `The table's expectations that DO hold for the Regulations as made and as amended`

-- In the table's own words (fork F11 for how they are read). The two that
-- do not hold are in tests-simplex-red.l4.
#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `registration approved` `holds for` `row 5 — registration for a theoretical exam` `under` `the regulations as made`
#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `registration approved` `holds for` `row 5 — registration for a theoretical exam` `under` `the regulations as amended`
#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `registration approved` `holds for` `row 6 — registration for a practical exam` `under` `the regulations as made`
#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `registration approved` `holds for` `row 6 — registration for a practical exam` `under` `the regulations as amended`
#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `the appeal is examined` `holds for` `row 7 — an appeal with payment of 40, on a theoretical exam` `under` `the regulations as made`
#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `the appeal is examined` `holds for` `row 7 — an appeal with payment of 40, on a theoretical exam` `under` `the regulations as amended`
#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `the appeal is examined` `holds for` `row 7 — an appeal with payment of 40, on a practical exam` `under` `the regulations as made`
#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `the appeal is examined` `holds for` `row 7 — an appeal with payment of 40, on a practical exam` `under` `the regulations as amended`
#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `suspension of service` `holds for` `row 8 — registration for a theoretical exam without payment` `under` `the regulations as amended`
#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `suspension of service` `holds for` `row 8 — registration for a practical exam without payment` `under` `the regulations as made`
#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `suspension of service` `holds for` `row 8 — registration for a practical exam without payment` `under` `the regulations as amended`
#ASSERT `the table's expectation` `registration rejected — payment must be completed` `holds for` `the worked example — a candidate registers for a theoretical exam but does not pay the fee` `under` `the regulations as amended`

-- The table's reference column does not survive into the enacted text: the
-- theoretical exam is 2(א1), not 2(א); the practical exam 2(א), not 2(ב); the
-- objection 2(ב), not 2(ג). Asserted above under "which sub-regulation".

§§ `Regulation 4 — the boundary and the draft's limits`

`a practical exam, 193 paid` MEANS
    Request WITH
        `the service requested` IS `taking` `a practical exam`
        `the amount paid`       IS 193

`a practical exam, 194 paid` MEANS
    Request WITH
        `the service requested` IS `taking` `a practical exam`
        `the amount paid`       IS 194

`a licence, nothing paid` MEANS
    Request WITH
        `the service requested` IS `a licence, or the renewal of one, under section 5`
        `the amount paid`       IS 0

`a theoretical exam, 100 of the draft's 273 paid` MEANS
    Request WITH
        `the service requested` IS `taking` `a theoretical exam`
        `the amount paid`       IS 100

`a temporary licence for a foreign expert, nothing paid` MEANS
    Request WITH
        `the service requested` IS `a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or the renewal of one, under section 9`
        `the amount paid`       IS 0

`a course under section 17, nothing paid` MEANS
    Request WITH
        `the service requested` IS `a continuing-training course under section 17`
        `the amount paid`       IS 0

-- "שילם את האגרה במלואה": paid in full; one shekel short is not.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `a practical exam, 193 paid` `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS `withheld: the fee set for the service was not paid in full`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `a practical exam, 194 paid` `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS `not withheld: the fee set for the service was paid in full`

-- "הרשם לא ייתן רישיון שנקבעה בעדו אגרה ... ולא יחדשו": an unpaid licence is
-- withheld as made and as amended.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `a licence, nothing paid` `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS `withheld: the fee set for the service was not paid in full`
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `a licence, nothing paid` `under` `the regulations as amended` EQUALS `withheld: the fee set for the service was not paid in full`
#ASSERT `the office regulation 4 binds for` `a licence, or the renewal of one, under section 5` EQUALS `the Registrar`
#ASSERT `the office regulation 4 binds for` (`taking` `a practical exam`) EQUALS `the Division for vocational training`

-- The temporary licence's fee is "בעד בקשה" (for the application), and reg 4
-- speaks of "רישיון שנקבעה בעדו אגרה": read as reaching it (fork F7).
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `a temporary licence for a foreign expert, nothing paid` `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS `withheld: the fee set for the service was not paid in full`

-- A course under s. 17 has no fee and is not among reg 4's services.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — what it does to` `a course under section 17, nothing paid` `under` `the regulations as made` EQUALS `not reached: no fee is set for the service`

-- The draft's reg 4 is not shown: beyond its gloss, the model declines.
#ASSERT REFUSED `regulation 4 — what it does to` `a licence, nothing paid` `under` `the draft` BECAUSE "the draft's regulation 4 is not shown, and its gloss reaches only registration for an exam with nothing paid"
#ASSERT REFUSED `regulation 4 — what it does to` `a theoretical exam, 100 of the draft's 273 paid` `under` `the draft` BECAUSE "the draft's regulation 4 is not shown, and its gloss reaches only registration for an exam with nothing paid"
#ASSERT REFUSED `regulation 4 — what it does to` `a course under section 17, nothing paid` `under` `the draft` BECAUSE "the draft's regulation 4 is not shown, and its gloss reaches only registration for an exam with nothing paid"

-- The prohibition, traced: the Division lets the unpaid practical exam go
-- ahead, and that is the breach.
#TRACE `regulation 4 — the prohibition on` `row 8 — registration for a practical exam without payment` `under` `the regulations as made` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Division for vocational training` DOES `allow the exam to be taken` AT 3

§§ `Regulation 3 — updating the fees`

#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest whole new shekel` 199.5 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest whole new shekel` 199.49 EQUALS 199
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the amount` 194 `updated by the change from` 100 `to` 103 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the update day of` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
#ASSERT `the first update day after the Regulations came into force` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
-- "המדד שפורסם בחודש שלפני תחילתן": the month before July 2025 is June 2025.
#ASSERT DATE_MONTH `the month before the Regulations came into force` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT DATE_YEAR `the month before the Regulations came into force` EQUALS 2025

-- Made-up index figures, to exercise the arithmetic only. No real figure is
-- in the sources.
`illustrative index figures` MEANS
    LIST (`Index publication` OF 2025, 6, 100)
       , (`Index publication` OF 2025, 11, 102)
       , (`Index publication` OF 2026, 11, 105)

-- 2025: as printed. 1 Jan 2026: 194 × 102/100 = 197.88 → 198.
-- 1 Jan 2027: 198 × 105/102 = 203.82… → 204.
#ASSERT `the fee payable for` (`taking` `a practical exam`) `on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `using the index figures` `illustrative index figures` EQUALS JUST 194
#ASSERT `the fee payable for` (`taking` `a practical exam`) `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `using the index figures` `illustrative index figures` EQUALS JUST 198
#ASSERT `the fee payable for` (`taking` `a practical exam`) `on` (YMD 2027 3 1) `using the index figures` `illustrative index figures` EQUALS JUST 204
-- 2(א1) is first updated on 1 Jan 2027, from the November 2025 figure:
-- 158 × 105/102 = 162.64… → 163.
#ASSERT `the fee payable for` (`taking` `a theoretical exam`) `on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `using the index figures` `illustrative index figures` EQUALS JUST 158
#ASSERT `the fee payable for` (`taking` `a theoretical exam`) `on` (YMD 2027 3 1) `using the index figures` `illustrative index figures` EQUALS JUST 163
-- Before 4 May 2026 (assumed) the text as made governs: no theoretical fee.
#ASSERT `the fee payable for` (`taking` `a theoretical exam`) `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `using the index figures` `illustrative index figures` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Before 16 July 2025 there were no Fees Regulations.
#ASSERT `the fee payable for` (`taking` `a practical exam`) `on` (YMD 2025 7 15) `using the index figures` `illustrative index figures` EQUALS NOTHING
-- With no figures supplied, a fee after 1 Jan 2026 cannot be computed.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the fee payable for` (`taking` `a practical exam`) `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `using the index figures` (LIST (`Index publication` OF 2030, 1, 1))) BECAUSE "an index figure that regulation 3 needs was not supplied"

-- The draft's reg 3 is not shown.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the draft's regulation 3 is not shown in the screenshot` EQUALS 0) BECAUSE "the draft's regulation 3 is not shown in the screenshot"

§§ `Regulation 5 — commencement, and the text in force on a day`

#ASSERT `the day the Regulations as made came into force` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT `the Fees Regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 7 15) EQUALS `no Fees Regulations were yet in force`
#ASSERT `the Fees Regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS `in force` `the regulations as made`
#ASSERT `the Fees Regulations in force on` (YMD 2026 5 3) EQUALS `in force` `the regulations as made`
#ASSERT `the Fees Regulations in force on` (YMD 2026 5 4) EQUALS `in force` `the regulations as amended`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the draft's commencement provision is not shown in the screenshot` EQUALS YMD 2025 1 1) BECAUSE "the draft's commencement provision is not shown in the screenshot"
